   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Dear Lola,</div><div><br></div><div>you write that you conducted CFAs already. </div><div>If those converged without problems, why not try the full longitudinal model and see what happens? Yes, the longitudinal model will be more complex (although you may include invariance constraints), but it will also contain more information.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,<br>Heiko</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><br></div><div><br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\"><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lolaa...@gmail.com</a> schrieb am Sonntag, 15. Juni 2025 um 10:51:33 UTC+2:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><p style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:medium;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">Dear all,</span></p><p style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:medium;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">I am working on a longitudinal study involving a <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">psychological intervention for individuals with chronic pain</span></strong><b>.</b> Participants were randomly assigned to either an <strong>intervention group (n = 81)</strong> or a <strong>waitlist control group (n = 82)</strong>. </span><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">Data were collected at three timepoints:</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">       </span></span><strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">T1</span></strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">: Baseline</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">       </span></span><strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">T2</span></strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">: 8-week post-treatment</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">       </span></span><strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">T3</span></strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">: 3-month follow-up</span></p><p style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:medium;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">I am interested in testing <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">mediation mechanisms of intervention effects overtime</span></strong><b> </b>using</span><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;font-weight:normal\"> </span></strong><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;font-weight:normal\">lavaan</span></strong><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">.</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:medium;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">Key constructs:</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">       </span></span><strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">Predictor</span></strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">: Group (0 = waitlist, 1 = intervention)</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">       </span></span><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">Mediator</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">: Perceived Stress Scale (PSS, 10 items)</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">       </span></span><strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">Outcome</span></strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">: Depression (PHQ, 9 items)</span></p><p style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:medium;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">Each construct is available as:</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">       </span></span><strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">Sum scores</span></strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">       </span></span><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">Item-level data</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\"><br>I conducted <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">CFAs</span></strong> on each scale individually with good model fit and internal consistency, and established <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">scalar invariance across timepoints</span></strong><b>.</b></span></p><p style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:medium;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">My questions:</span></b></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">1.<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">     </span></span><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">Feasibility of using sum scores for mediation models:</span></strong><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\"><br></span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">My understanding is that modeling all constructs as latent variables at the item level (i.e., three latent variables per construct across time) may be <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">too complex</span></strong> given my sample size.</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:72pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">o<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">   </span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">Would it be acceptable to test <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">longitudinal mediation</span></strong><b> </b>using <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">sum scores</span></strong><b> </b>(i.e., as a<b> </b>path model) in a framework such as<b> </b><strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">CLPM</span></strong><b>, </b><strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">RI-CLPM</span></strong><b>, </b>or <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Latent Growth Curve Mediation</span></strong><b>?</b></span></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">2.<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">     </span></span><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">Alternatives to full latent modeling:</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\"><br>If full item-level latent modeling is not advisable, what are your thoughts on alternatives such as:</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:72pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">o<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">   </span></span><strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black;font-weight:normal\">Parceling items</span></strong><b><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\"></span></b></p><p style=\"margin-left:72pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">o<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">   </span></span><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black;font-weight:normal\">Estimating factor scores</span></strong><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\"> </span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">and applying <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Croon’s correction</span></strong><b> </b>in mediation paths<b></b></span></p><p style=\"margin-left:72pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">o<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">   </span></span><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black;font-weight:normal\">Modeling only one construct as latent</span></strong><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\"> </span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">(e.g., the mediator), while treating<b> </b>predictor and outcome as manifest<b></b></span></p><p style=\"margin-left:36pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">3.<span style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">     </span></span><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">Less complex options for testing longitudinal mediation:</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\"><br>Are there less complex yet valid approaches to test mediation over time?<br>For example, is it acceptable to model <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">PSS_T2 as a mediator</span></strong> of the intervention’s effect on <strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">PHQ_T3</span></strong><b>,</b> controlling for PHQ_T1 an PSS_T1 and maybe controlling for PSS_T2 in lavaan?</span></p><p style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:medium;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">I would be very grateful for your feedback on which modeling strategy is most appropriate and feasible in this context.</span></p><p style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:medium;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">Kind regards, </span></p><p style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:medium;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">Lola </span></p></blockquote></div>"
    ]
